  "lookup_contract": {
    "description": "The lookup contract (ADR 0015): the documented order active, withdrawn, non-ISO decides which entry currency() returns (the earliest section wins); within one section the last entry for a code wins and the collection has one entry per code; Python and JavaScript raise TypeError for a code argument that is not a string. Go and Rust cannot be given one. v1.9.6 adds the lookups that take a country or anchor code (pegged_to, issued_by, used_in); invalid_input_count is the size of the group (methods times values), and method_applies_to, when it names a method, narrows applies_to for that method to the wrappers that guard it. Each wrapper builds the registries below through its own loader.",
