  "collection_order": {
    "description": "Collection order (v1.9.6): every collection is in file order, the order of the entries in iso4217.json, section by section, one entry per code. all_non_iso walks the categories cryptocurrencies, stablecoins, commodities, special_purpose in that order, whatever the key order of the object. all_currencies is active, then withdrawn, then non-ISO. A code listed more than once keeps the position of its first entry; the entry that wins is the one ADR 0015 names (the last within a section, the earliest section across sections). pegged_to keeps the order of all_active. 'shipped' is each wrapper's own copy of iso4217.json and is regenerated when that file changes (tests/test_wrapper_collection_order.py prints the expected lists); each 'synthetic' registry is built through each wrapper's own loader. Every wrapper compares its full code lists with these, so the four outputs are identical.",
